## Delivery summary

This sample applies the document preset to ordinary Mote content. The page uses a comfortable text width, dark body text, and consistent spacing. **Important findings** can be emphasized without changing the overall style.

The figures below are illustrative. Text columns are left aligned; numeric columns are right aligned. The table fills the text area without setting a width in the content file.

| Workstream | Completed | Planned | On time |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Research | 18 | 20 | 90% |
| Design | 24 | 24 | 100% |
| Engineering | 42 | 48 | 88% |
| Quality | 31 | 34 | 91% |
| Operations | 16 | 18 | 89% |
| Support | 27 | 30 | 90% |

#paragraph(style = "Caption")[Table 1. Illustrative delivery figures. Alternating rows help the reader follow each workstream across the page.]

### Priorities for the next cycle

- Finish the remaining engineering work before adding new scope.
- Review quality checks with the delivery team.
- Keep status reporting short enough to scan before each meeting.

### Authoring notes

Use `#import("defaults/document.mote")` before the content, with a path relative to your file. Markdown headings, lists, and tables inherit the preset.
